speechtext:
On a point of order, Mr. Chairman, may I call your attention to citation 293 in Beauchesne, paragraph (i):
(i) use his right of speech for the purpose of obstructing the business of the house;
A moment ago, Mr. Chairman, you told the hon. member that he had repeated the same arguments and re-read and quoted the same parts of speeches on questions that may be germane to this resolution; but ait the same time you called his attention to the terms of the resolution. For the last hour the hon. member has been obstructing the business of the house-and I call as my witnesses everybody sitting in this house- even when the minister tried his best to answer the questions that were put to him. I would like to see him kept in order, to see if we can have this debate concluded after two days.
